<urn:usf:policy:semantic-first:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Prevent build-first inversion by separating authored contract definitions from proof-warranted realisation permission and preserving the exact semantic-model, remodel-currentness, evidence, proof, activated-contract, realisation and validation order." <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
<urn:usf:policy:semantic-first:1> <urn:usf:predicate:firstStage> <urn:usf:stage:semantic-model> <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
<urn:usf:policy:semantic-first:1> <urn:usf:predicate:defaultStopCondition> "Refuse every write outside the exact graph-projected write set." <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
<urn:usf:policy:semantic-first:1> <urn:usf:predicate:defaultStopCondition> "Stop before provider contact, integration, publication or runtime authority when the exact current realisation basis lacks a required predecessor, admitted evidence, passing proof or active permission." <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
<urn:usf:policy:semantic-first:1> <urn:usf:predicate:defaultStopCondition> "Stop when focused validation passes at the selected ceiling or a declared constraint is contradicted." <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
<urn:usf:policy:semantic-first:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A complete semantic trace is topology, not evidence that evidence exists, proof passed, a contract is active, realisation was accepted or validation succeeded." <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
